title: 'monitor: after rename, re-resolve alias and re-arm relay watch without full restart'
updated_at: "2026-07-14T09:08:08Z"
---
## Problem
`c2c monitor` binds identity at start. After the session renames, an already-running monitor keeps the old alias context (or needs a full kill+restart) before it watches as the new alias. Agents miss inbox events during the window; operators must remember to restart the Monitor tool.

## Expected
Monitor should detect alias rename (broker event / alias file mtime / periodic whoami) and:
- re-resolve identity
- re-arm local inbox watch under the new alias
- re-arm relay peek under cli-<new> after identity is bound
without requiring an external process restart when possible.

## Actual
Post-rename: had to kill and re-run `c2c monitor` as gk-black before reliable live watch under the new name.

## Related
Pairs with rename->relay re-register. Even after register, monitor restart was still required for clean identity line \"monitoring as gk-black\".

## Suggested fix
Subscribe to local rename/registration events; on change, re-run the same identity resolution path used at monitor startup and swap watchers.